      "index": "b00",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 247064037,
      "version": 804,
      "versionNonce": 1276349445,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785753243005,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "So basically in execution context of javascript there are 2 phases \n\n1. memory creation where js engine creates the memory for the variables\n2. execution thread where js engine do the execution of the codes \n3.whenever a function is called js engine creates a new execution context after the execution and memory creation is finished in \nthat context the execution context get deleted.",
      "fontSize": 23.054545454545448,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "So basically in execution context of javascript there are 2 phases \n\n1. memory creation where js engine creates the memory for the variables\n2. execution thread where js engine do the execution of the codes \n3.whenever a function is called js engine creates a new execution context after the execution and memory creation is finished in \nthat context the execution context get deleted.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
